From 01f81f3ab9a0a85724a018ffc83a5d13069e855c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:25:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Desktop: resend an identityless prompt the rolled
 hub refused as "session not found"
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After a hub backend roll the first send in a hub chat failed with "Legacy submission
acknowledgement is unknown; automatic retry is unsafe" and the typed text was not sent
(David, 2026-11-13 12:05:43 and 12:06:37 PT; hub agent.log 20:05:40/20:06:36 UTC
`session-scoped RPC rejected: method=prompt.submit ... not in memory`, one prompt.submit each).

Problem: a send right after an instant core update rolled the hub's Desktop backend was dropped.
Why 1: the submit callback was re-entered by withSessionNotFoundResume with
  prepared.legacyAttempted already true, which throws by design (submit.ts:1203; bundle
  main-DqpORIB6.js:181 matches main).
Why 2: the first send was identityless and met the rolled backend's 4001 "session not found"
  (tui_gateway/session_registry.py `_sess_nowait`); isDefiniteSubmitRefusal reset
  legacyAttempted only for 4009, 4090 (not UNCONFIRMED) and 4094/4000+submission_id.
Why 3 (why identityless at all): the hub chat runs on the `hermes serve` sidecar, whose
  prompt.submit contract (tui_gateway/contracts/prompt_voice.py PromptSubmitParams) has no
  submission_id; rpc_dispatch.validate_params answers 4000 "submission_id: Extra inputs are not
  permitted" before any handler (reproduced), and Desktop remembers that per scope for 10 min
  (submission-identity-support.ts). So every hub-sidecar send is identityless by design.
Why 4: is 4001 a definite "nothing admitted"? Yes: prompt.submit looks the runtime up via
  `_sess_nowait` before the turn claim, user-row write, busy queue and owner forward; only
  note_submit (a human-input timestamp) and the typed voice-stop check run first, and the
  owner-forward path maps owner failures to 4090, never 4001. dispatch validates params and
  calls the handler, nothing else.
Root (happened): the definite-refusal list is hand-enumerated per incident; the sidecar's
  stale-runtime refusal — the one a backend roll guarantees — was never classified, so the
  recovery the 4001 asks for (resume + resend) always hit the duplicate-turn fence.
Root (not caught): no test drove an identityless send through withSessionNotFoundResume. The
  sleep/wake tests use identified sends; the legacy-identity tests cover 4090/4009 but not
  4001; nothing pinned the sidecar's 4001 frame as pre-admission.
Recurrence: the same class as ef7a9e6b2d (4090 refusal treated as unconfirmed, Nov 12);
  present since 41b017f1e3 (Sep 8) fenced legacy retries, made frequent by the hub's instant
  core updates (179 on 2026-11-13).

Fix: isStaleRuntimeRefusal — a JsonRpcGatewayError code 4001 whose message is exactly
"session not found" and that carries no reason — is a definite refusal, so legacyAttempted is
reset and the resume's resend goes out once. A codeless error, a 4001 with a canonical reason,
prose that only mentions the phrase, and timeouts/disconnects stay ambiguous (fence unchanged).

Tests:
- submit-backend-roll.test.tsx: identityless (remembered refusal and fresh client) and
  identified sends after a roll each land ONE turn with no visible failure (3 RED before the
  fix, GREEN after); four ambiguous shapes still refuse the automatic resend; an explicit retry
  after a 4001 whose resume failed resends once.
- tests/tui_gateway/test_prompt_submit_stale_runtime.py: the sidecar answers a stale runtime
  with the bare {4001, "session not found"} and writes nothing; the contract refuses
  submission_id with 4000 before any handler.

Deferred: identity (dedupe) for sidecar prompt.submit is a separate design (needs durable
dedupe across rolls); this change makes the identityless path safe to retry.
